# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Paul L. Houston et al. (2024). No Headache for PIPs: A PIP Potential for Aspirin Runs Much Faster and with Similar Precision Than Other Machine-Learned Potentials.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.4c00054  arXiv:2401.09316v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2401.09316v1 (sha256 a67997216e9e1e5b...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 569 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/houston2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: PIP fits to rMD17 aspirin (third-order basis with
# 49,978 coefficients; a 25,001-coefficient 2-4 order basis for PES1):
# the train/test study with three training sizes (Table 2) and the four
# final PESs fitted to the lowest-energy data (Table 3). Errors are in
# cm-1 and cm-1/bohr (outside the schema units) and kept with unit null.
# Literature ACE, PaiNN and Allegro values and stationary-point
# properties are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-houston2024 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Houston et al. (2024): a permutationally invariant polynomial potential for aspirin with precision similar to other MLPs and much faster evaluation" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-houston2024 .

